    "summary": "loadAnalyzeConfig/resolveTier resolve each global tier through an injectable registry (default getModelRegistry()): an unset or '' tier takes the default family's tier default with its effort, aliases become canonical ids, an unaccepted effort is dropped and a rejected or unlisted model falls back (decision A), each logged with a warning; AnalyzeConfig.tierResolutions keeps each tier's resolution. TierEffort is EffortLevel, runners are FamilyId, per-repo entries keep only tasks and coreFloor. A '' model stays an unset tier (as before), so shaperProviderExplicit keeps its client auto-pick behaviour for configs whose core model is ''.",
